        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "Aye, I've seen the lad -- flour still under his nails, trailing after black-robed men like a duckling after foxes. *He shifts his pack.* Roads are thin fare for a peddler, friend. A coin for the telling? Or a kind word, at least, to carry me over the bridge."
          }
        }
      },
